{"id": "EUVD-2026-86854", "enisaUuid": "2bdd0f31-8f05-3447-bacf-54404f029e68", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: don't spin forever on zero-length dirents when salvaging them\n\nLOLLM noticed that xrep_dir_recover_data can spin forever if it\nencounters an unused dirent that claims to have length zero.  Fix that,\nand prevent the same thing from happening with a zero-length entry.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:09", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5442f0c56445618544a801fb4dae35aed87a1aaa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08754ebfa5c28e8d57316b1bd7a5a921a5e2e762", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a455c83ce5dc1a2da33b1b84253d298372a8dfbd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9f84792b40d0c96833341602144574bf0bd14a6a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-56gf-pmq5-4wg3", "CVE-2026-97546"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b5d24b6-46fb-3fcb-aa45-383847f846e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b1991ee3e7cf852e95a3498801303cfbb4468681 <a455c83ce5dc1a2da33b1b84253d298372a8dfbd"}, {"id": "5adaacc7-34d8-3577-a88b-1a2aca38468b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "61289163-54b5-3a2e-a4b2-9ea7b067cc12", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b1991ee3e7cf852e95a3498801303cfbb4468681 <5442f0c56445618544a801fb4dae35aed87a1aaa"}, {"id": "812cc0ff-ee8b-3dbb-97f5-16c7bc106bce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "85a702fc-8443-33b6-a1b1-8ce33015d488", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "95d1ec29-b729-317d-a766-71df052f0c60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b1991ee3e7cf852e95a3498801303cfbb4468681 <9f84792b40d0c968